5,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzA5ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2230985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312","html_url":"https://github.com/connor4312","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/connor4312/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I would like to request a feature that enables GitHub Copilot to be triggered programmatically via a hook in agent mode (or similar automation-friendly mode). The core idea is to allow Copilot to generate code or documentation based on the current state of the project automatically, without manual intervention.\n\n**My Use Case**\n\nIn my development workflow, I want to automatically generate documentation or helper code just before pushing a commit to a remote repository. Ideally, this would happen inside a pre-push or pre-commit Git hook.\nI store instructions in a `.github/copilot/` directory and then point to this directory in the configuration like. So this feature also should be aware of it:\n```json\n    \"github.copilot.chat.codeGeneration.instructions\": [\n        {\n            \"file\": \".github/copilot/code-generation-instructions.md\",\n        },\n        {\n            \"file\": \".github/copilot/me.md\",\n        }\n    ],\n```\n\nFor example:\n\t•\tI finish implementing a new feature.\n\t•\tBefore pushing the code, I want a script to trigger Copilot to generate a documentation snippet summarizing the purpose and behavior of that feature (e.g., in a docstring or Markdown format).\n\t•\tThis generation would be handled through Copilot’s LLM engine, acting as an agent that understands context and can generate appropriate outputs.\n\n**Problem**\n\nCurrently, Copilot requires a manual interaction inside the editor (e.g., prompting via inline suggestion or chat), which makes it hard to integrate into automated or semi-automated development pipelines. There’s no accessible API or CLI interface to trigger Copilot generation headlessly.\n\n**Proposed Solution**\n\nIntroduce a hook-friendly interface for Copilot, such as:\n\t•\tA CLI or API endpoint for initiating generation requests.\n\t•\tA background “agent mode” that listens to triggers and produces output based on context (e.g., file diffs, commit messages, or staged code).\n\t•\tThe ability to specify generation type (e.g., documentation, test cases, comments) and target location (inline, separate file, etc.).\n\n**Why This Matters**\n\nThis would enable powerful automation scenarios such as:\n\t•\tCI/CD pipelines enriched with AI-generated documentation or tests.\n\t•\tDeveloper workflows that reduce manual context-switching.\n\t•\tTeams enforcing a minimum documentation standard automatically.\n\nI believe this feature aligns with Copilot’s mission to be a true coding assistant and not just a reactive tool. Let me know if this is feasible or if there’s already something experimental in that direction.","closed_by":{"login":"roblourens","id":323878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzg3OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens","html_url":"https://github.com/roblourens","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/10161/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/10161/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null},"comments":[]}